<title>BELGIUM: Gain boosts Royale Belge 1996 profit.</title>
<headline>Gain boosts Royale Belge 1996 profit.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in billions of Belgian francs unless stated):</p>
<p>    Group net profit		 11.315  vs   6.176</p>
<p>    Extraordinary gain *	    4.225  vs   nil</p>
<p>    Current profit		    7.090  vs   6.176</p>
<p>    Gross dividend (francs)	   293  vs     260</p>
<p>    Bonus dividend (francs)	    67  vs   nil</p>
<p>NOTE - Royale Belge, Belgium's second largest insurance company, is controlled jointly by French insurance group AXA-UAP and Belgium's Groupe Bruxelles Lambert. * gain from sale of stake in Tractebel.</p>
<p>Breakdown of results according to country, sector:</p>
<p>Insurance</p>
<p>- Belgium/Luxembourg</p>
<p>    Current profit		    6.232  vs   5.633</p>
<p>    Exceptional gain		  4.225  vs   nil</p>
<p>- Netherlands</p>
<p>    Current profit		    0.129  vs   0.006</p>
<p>    Exceptional loss/transfer     0.247  vs   nil</p>
<p>    Other income			0.447  vs   0.323</p>
<p>     Ippa Bank			0.529  vs   0.214</p>
<p>Cons premium income</p>
<p>    - Life			     46.702  vs  44.787</p>
<p>    of which Belgium		 24.657  vs  23.802</p>
<p>		 Netherlands	   17.980  vs  17.639</p>
<p>		 Luxembourg	     2.994  vs   2.512</p>
<p>    - Non-life			 65.734  vs  64.566</p>
<p>    of which Belgium		 37.603  vs  37.396</p>
<p>		 Netherlands	   21.357  vs  21.457</p>
<p>		 Luxembourg	     1.368  vs   1.115</p>
<p>    Commissions - Belgium	   0.091  vs   0.122</p>
<p>		    - Netherlands     1.674  vs   1.645</p>
<p>    Banking income - Belgium	7.320  vs   6.273</p>
<p>Royale Belge said in a statement that profit from its Dutch operation was affected by an exceptional increase of life policy reserves linked to the increasingly ageing population. The company said that under Belgian accounting law this had to be treated as an exceptional loss/transfer.</p>
<p>Royale Belge's share of profit from Belgian bank BBL, in which it has a 12.4 percent stake, made up the bulk of the rise to 6.232 billion francs in current profit from its Belgian operations.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
